<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Guelph Community Gardens &mdash; OSM Coverage Gaps</title>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="../index.css">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="gaps.css">
<link rel="stylesheet"
      href="https://unpkg.com/leaflet@1.9.4/dist/leaflet.css"
      integrity="sha256-p4NxAoJBhIIN+hmNHrzRCf9tD/miZyoHS5obTRR9BMY="
      crossorigin="">
<script defer src="https://unpkg.com/leaflet@1.9.4/dist/leaflet.js"
        integrity="sha256-20nQCchB9co0qIjJZRGuk2/Z9VM+kNiyxNV1lvTlZBo="
        crossorigin=""></script>
<script defer src="gaps.js"></script>
</head>
<body class="app">

<header class="bar">
  <div class="bar-head">
    <h1>Guelph Community Gardens &mdash; OSM coverage gaps</h1>
    <a class="back" href="../">&larr; reference layer</a>
    <a class="back" href="history.html">gaps over time &rarr;</a>
  </div>
  <div class="counts">
    <div class="count missing"><strong>{{MISSING_COUNT}}</strong><span>missing in OSM</span></div>
    <div class="count point_only"><strong>{{POINT_ONLY_COUNT}}</strong><span>no City footprint, not in OSM</span></div>
    <div class="count untyped"><strong>{{UNTYPED_COUNT}}</strong><span>OSM garden untyped</span></div>
    <div class="count unnamed"><strong>{{UNNAMED_COUNT}}</strong><span>OSM garden unnamed</span></div>
    <div class="count name_mismatch"><strong>{{NAME_MISMATCH_COUNT}}</strong><span>name mismatches</span></div>
    <div class="count"><strong>{{MATCHED_COUNT}}</strong><span>matched cleanly</span></div>
    <div class="count"><strong>{{CITY_COUNT}}</strong><span>City food gardens</span></div>
    <div class="count pollinator"><strong>{{POLLINATOR_COUNT}}</strong><span>pollinator patches (not counted)</span></div>
    <div class="count"><strong>{{OSM_COUNT}}</strong><span>OSM gardens</span></div>
    <div class="count meta-count">City roster {{POINTS_DATE}} &middot; footprints {{POLYGONS_DATE}} &middot; OSM data {{OSM_DATE}} &middot; compared {{BUILD_DATE}}</div>
  </div>
  {{OSM_NOTE}}
  <p class="licence">
    <a href="{{LICENSE_URL}}">{{LICENSE_NOTICE}}</a>
    Sources: <a href="{{POINTS_PAGE}}">Community Gardens</a> (the roster) and
    <a href="{{POLYGONS_PAGE}}">Community Gardens Polygons</a> (footprints).
  </p>
</header>

<div class="layout">
  <div id="gap-map"
       data-geojson="gaps.geojson"
       data-raster="../tiles/raster/{z}/{x}/{y}.png"></div>

  <aside class="panel">
    <div class="panel-head">
      <div class="controls">
        <label><span class="swatch missing"></span>
          <input type="checkbox" id="show-missing" checked> Missing</label>
        <label><span class="swatch point_only"></span>
          <input type="checkbox" id="show-point_only" checked> Point only</label>
        <label><span class="swatch untyped"></span>
          <input type="checkbox" id="show-untyped" checked> Untyped</label>
        <label><span class="swatch unnamed"></span>
          <input type="checkbox" id="show-unnamed" checked> Unnamed</label>
        <label><span class="swatch name_mismatch"></span>
          <input type="checkbox" id="show-name_mismatch" checked> Name mismatch</label>
        <label><span class="swatch pollinator"></span>
          <input type="checkbox" id="show-pollinator"> Pollinator</label>
        <input type="search" id="filter" placeholder="Filter by name...">
      </div>
      <details class="hint">
        <summary>How to read this, and what to map</summary>
        <p>
          Green shapes and dots are the City's gardens (raster layer); coloured
          dots flag the gaps. Click a row to outline it on the map, then press
          <kbd>O</kbd> to open it on openstreetmap.org or <kbd>I</kbd> in the iD
          editor.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Treat the City's outline as a hint, not a trace.</strong> Many
          footprints are a single bed &mdash; the median is about 230&nbsp;m&sup2;
          &mdash; and the layer has not been redrawn since mid-2025. Map what is on
          the ground or in current imagery: usually <code>leisure=garden</code> +
          <code>garden:type=community</code> around the whole plot area, with the
          name on the sign.
        </p>
        <p>
          A garden counts as mapped when any OSM <code>leisure=garden</code>,
          <code>landuse=allotments</code> or <code>landuse=orchard</code> lies
          within {{RADIUS}}&nbsp;m of its outline (or of its roster point when the
          City has drawn no outline). Each OSM garden is matched to at most one
          City garden, so two City gardens side by side need two OSM gardens.
          <strong>Missing</strong>: nothing near the outline.
          <strong>Point only</strong>: nothing near, and the City has no outline
          either &mdash; the newest gardens; find them on the ground.
          <strong>Untyped</strong>: matched to a plain <code>leisure=garden</code>;
          check it is the community garden, then add
          <code>garden:type=community</code>.
          <strong>Unnamed</strong> / <strong>name mismatch</strong>: the OSM garden
          has no name, or another one.
        </p>
        <p>
          Names are the City's ALL CAPS roster names, title-cased here; check the
          sign before copying one. <strong>Pollinator</strong> patches are on the
          City's roster too, but OpenStreetMap has no settled tag for a pollinator
          garden, so they are listed (off by default) and never counted as gaps.
        </p>
      </details>
    </div>
    <div class="table-scroll">
      <table id="gap-table">
        <thead>
          <tr><th class="col-name">Garden (City roster)</th><th>Address</th>
              <th>Status</th><th>OSM &middot; iD</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody></tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </aside>
</div>

</body>
</html>
